FILE: examples/modal/index.html, examples/modal/main.js, examples/modal/README.md
FEATURE: example-redesign
DATE: 2026-08-26
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'modal-example-expansion'

OLD_SECTION
index.html — 158 lines: sans-serif body, <fieldset>/<legend> groups, grey #f0f0f0 log,
             light modal blocks with coloured top borders, a gradient .filler.
main.js    — 74 lines: two instances, an effect <select>, an overlay-type <select>,
             a delegated .close-all handler.

NEW_SECTION
index.html — 362 lines: shared design system plus a hero, five numbered sections
             (effects & overlay, stacking, widths & instances, bad input, scroll),
             a depth readout with a colour key, and dark modal blocks.
main.js    — 176 lines: the same two instances, plus live config for effect,
             overlayBackgroundType, overlayStyle (colour + alpha), exitOnAway and
             screenBreakPoints; a generated code panel; and ten validation demos.

REASON
Brings the page up to the standard in CLAUDE.md. Every demonstration the old page made is
kept — the three-layer stack, the second instance sharing one stack, closeAll() from
inside a modal, self-stacking being ignored, per-trigger widths, the tall modal, the
open/close processors, the depth counter and the scroll-position proof — and the gaps the
standard names are filled:

  - Lead with the component: the hero opens a real dialog rather than describing one.
  - Interactive: five config properties were previously fixed in code; all are now live
    controls, with a code panel showing the equivalent configuration.
  - Failure modes: a new section performs ten bad calls and prints what was thrown.

Two structural points the redesign had to respect, both now stated in comments and in the
README rather than left to be rediscovered:

  - Modal content is MOVED into the component's overlay, which is appended to <body>.
    Those blocks are therefore styled standalone, not as descendants of the page wrapper.
  - #page (config.pageContainer for the blur mode) deliberately does not wrap the modal
    content, or the dialog would blur along with the page behind it.

One demo was dropped rather than restyled: an "open before initialize()" button. The
guard it would have shown lives in a private show() function reachable only through a
trigger click, and an uninitialised instance has no click listener attached — so the
error cannot be produced from outside the component, and a button claiming to produce it
would have been a lie. Replaced with 'className = 42', which genuinely throws.

VERIFICATION
All ten error demos were checked against the real helpers from src/helpers.js with the
exact values the page passes, together with the values the page actually uses, to confirm
the live configuration is not itself invalid: 14 assertions, all passing. Every id and
data-attribute selector in main.js was cross-checked against the markup (15 ids, 10 error
buttons, 7 modal ids, all trigger/close classes), and the page was served over HTTP.
